<Base title="Leadership"><Heading label="Make room for others" title="Leadership starts with paying attention." description="I try to understand what someone needs to contribute: a clear next step, a connection, encouragement, or space to work independently."/><section class="section"><div class="two-col"><h2>Guide. Connect.<br/>Then listen again.</h2><div><p>At Venture Studio, a student’s idea could need expertise I did not have. At Uplift, a volunteer needed to understand how their contribution fit into the program. Those experiences taught me to respond to the person and the situation.</p><p>I am learning to balance initiative with listening, and ambition with the practical work of following through.</p><p class="source">Adapted from personal reflections, brag sheet pp. 18–19, 23–24, 26–27.</p></div></div></section><OpportunityDiagram/><section class="section"><h2>Leadership through the work.</h2>{projects.map(p=><article class="list-row"><div><p class="eyebrow">{p.area}</p><h3>{p.title}</h3></div><div><p>{p.contribution}</p><a class="small-link" href={path(`projects/${p.slug}/`)}>Read the account →</a></div></article>)}</section><section class="section"><h2>Diplomacy & student communities.</h2><div class="two-col"><div><h3>Model United Nations</h3><p>I cochaired the Security Council and supported conference operations at GUAMUN in January 2024. Across Model UN experiences, I practiced research, negotiation, fair participation, and public speaking.</p><p class="source">Brag sheet pp. 10, 13–14. The source varies on the precise human-resources title, so that title is not asserted here.</p></div><div><h3>National Economics Club</h3><p>The source describes my work as president developing recruitment, economic education, and preparation for the National Economics Challenge and National Personal Finance Challenge.</p><p class="source">The approximately 100-member figure is a recruitment target, not achieved membership. Brag sheet pp. 6–7.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Professional experience.</h2><p>Roles described in the supplied material; employment dates and current status are not independently confirmed.</p>{roles.map(([org,role,text])=><article class="list-row"><div><h3>{org}</h3><span class="meta">{role}</span></div><p>{text}</p></article>)}<p class="source">Source: brag sheet pp. 7–9. No confidential client information is included.</p></section><a href={path('journal/?category=Speaking')}>Speaking & public communication →</a></Base>
